env-doctor: The AI Environment Fixer

positional arguments:
  {check,cuda-info,cuda-install,cudnn-info,wsl,dockerfile,docker-compose,python-compat,install,scan,debug,model,export,validate,init,dashboard,report}
                        Available commands
    check               Diagnose environment compatibility
    cuda-info           Detailed CUDA toolkit analysis
    cuda-install        Step-by-step CUDA Toolkit installation guide
    cudnn-info          Detailed cuDNN library analysis
    wsl                 Detailed WSL environment analysis
    dockerfile          Validate Dockerfile for GPU/CUDA configuration issues
    docker-compose      Validate docker-compose.yml for GPU configuration issues
    python-compat       Check Python version compatibility with AI libraries
    install             Get safe installation command for a library
    scan                Scan local files for AI library imports
    debug               Show detailed detector information (for troubleshooting)
    model               Check if AI model fits on your GPU
    export              Export environment as a shareable JSON spec
    validate            Validate current environment against a spec file
    init                Generate CI/CD integration files
    dashboard           Start the web dashboard server
    report              Manage periodic reporting to a dashboard

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit

Examples:
  env-doctor check              # Diagnose your environment
  env-doctor cuda-info          # Detailed CUDA toolkit analysis
  env-doctor cuda-install       # Step-by-step CUDA installation guide
  env-doctor cuda-install 12.4  # Install specific CUDA version
  env-doctor cudnn-info         # Detailed cuDNN library analysis
  env-doctor wsl                # Detailed WSL environment analysis
  env-doctor dockerfile         # Validate Dockerfile for GPU issues
  env-doctor docker-compose     # Validate docker-compose.yml for GPU issues
  env-doctor model llama-3-8b   # Check if model fits on your GPU
  env-doctor model --list       # List all available models
  env-doctor python-compat      # Check Python version compatibility
  env-doctor install torch      # Get safe install command for PyTorch
  env-doctor scan               # Scan project for AI library imports
  env-doctor debug              # Show detailed detector information
  env-doctor export             # Export environment as shareable JSON spec
  env-doctor validate spec.json # Validate environment against a spec
  env-doctor dashboard          # Start web dashboard for fleet monitoring
  env-doctor report install     # Set up periodic reporting to a dashboard
        

